# Local settings for the HPC precompile scripts. Copy to hpc/local.conf, which
# is gitignored, and edit. Nothing here is committed: an account name, a login
# node and a path on your own disk are not the repository's business, and this
# keeps them out of it.
#
#   cp hpc/local.conf.example hpc/local.conf
#
# Every setting can also be given as an environment variable, which takes
# precedence over this file.

# The cluster, as ssh would take it. Required.
HOST=you@login-node.example.org

# Where the job directory goes on the cluster. Defaults to
# /export/scratch/<the account in HOST>/bayesnec-precompile.
#DEST=/export/scratch/you/bayesnec-precompile

# The container image on this machine. Needed to build it, and to copy it to the
# cluster the first time. Once the cluster holds an image matching
# hpc/image.lock, a precompile run needs no local copy and this can stay unset.
#
# Under WSL, build it somewhere other than the repository: the repository is on
# a 9p mount where unpacking the base image takes an order of magnitude longer.
#SIF=/home/you/tmp/bayesnec-precompile.sif

# Where apptainer unpacks the base image while building. About 15GB, and it must
# be a local Linux filesystem -- build.sh refuses a tmpfs or a 9p mount.
#APPTAINER_TMPDIR=/home/you/tmp/apptainer
